  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member whose pseudo contains a space, or another character that `md_user` URL-encodes, I want my own posts and the quotes of my posts highlighted, so that the reader shows them as it does for every other member.\n\n### Scope\n- `VisibilityPolicy.init(ownPseudo:)` (`App/SwiftHFR/Reader/VisibilityPolicy.swift:51-53`) builds `ownKey` from `PseudoNormalizer.comparisonForm(ownPseudo)`.\n- The pseudo it receives is the account key, i.e. the raw `md_user` value: `AppEnvironment.make` passes `accountName` to `ReaderSettings.live(pseudo:)`, and `ReaderSettings.visibility` hands it to `VisibilityPolicy`.\n- That value is URL-encoded (HFR-PROTOCOL §5, `W03`; `AccountsModelLoginTests` stores `user%20two` for \"user two\"). So \"user two\" never matches their own posts (`.own`, class `me`) nor the quotes of their posts (`.ofMe`).\n- LOT-159 (#1290) fixed the same class in `PseudoListManager.isOwn` with `PseudoListManager.keyForms(of:)`, which compares the raw and the percent-decoded key, as `AccountBook.checkSessionCookie` does. Fix: reuse it in `VisibilityPolicy`, or pass the account's display name.\n\n### Blocked by\n#1290\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A test with the account key `user%20two` finds \"user two\"'s post as `.own` and a quote of \"user two\" as `.ofMe`. It fails before the fix.\n- [ ] Accented pseudos stay pending capture: how `md_user` encodes accents is not captured yet (LOT-159 spec, Edge cases).\n\nFound by the adversarial review of #1290 (Fable 5.2, r1290), round 1, finding 1.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
